                <pb facs="0415" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 30, 1890</date>.
                        (Received July 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In transmitting to the Department a copy
                    and translation of the note of Freiherr von Marschall, dated the 23d instant,
                    covering the copies which he has sent us of the various decrees affecting the
                    importation into the German Empire of horned cattle, hogs, and hogs’ meat of
                    American origin, you will notice that he explains and excuses such legislation
                    “on account of the diseases of cattle existing in the United States.”</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Walter
                    Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>














